# CO-QA-001 — Enterprise Regression Certification Standard

Status: **ENTERPRISE APPROVED** · Effective immediately · Permanent  
Sprint / Standard ID: **CO-QA-001**

## Effective immediately

Every Business Certified module must include **at least one real end-to-end business scenario**.

Whenever any **related domain** changes, that scenario **must be re-run**.

## What does NOT grant Business Certification

Business Certification is **NOT** granted solely based on:

- Successful build  
- TypeScript  
- Lint  
- Verify scripts  
- Smoke tests  

These are **engineering gates only**.

## What grants Business Certification readiness

Business Certification requires **successful execution** of the defined end-to-end scenario on the live certification / production application.

Product Owner may then explicitly accept (“Business Certified”). Until then, agents may only claim Ready / Partially Ready / Requires Further Development per `business-functional-certification-report.mdc`.

## Failure rule (non-negotiable)

If the end-to-end scenario **fails**, the module remains **OPEN** regardless of technical verification status (build / TypeScript / lint / verify / smoke).

Do **not** close the sprint, mark Ready for Business Certification, or imply certification while the Scenario Pack is Fail or not yet run.

## Related domain change → mandatory re-run

Re-run the module’s Scenario Pack before claiming Ready / Certified when changes touch:

- Persistence, purge, storage keys, migrations  
- Association / ownership / identity keys  
- Registry / API list filters  
- Hydration / projection adapters  
- Cross-entity linkage (Document / Task / Deal / Opportunity / Contact)  
- Navigation or workspace entry that loads the entity  

A prior Pass is **invalidated** until the scenario is re-run and Passes again.

## Scenario Pack (required artefact)

Every Business Certified (or BAT-bound) module must maintain:

`docs/<module-or-sprint>/<MODULE>-E2E-SCENARIO.md`

Template: `docs/governance/E2E-BUSINESS-SCENARIO-PACK-TEMPLATE.md`  
Programme docs: `docs/co-qa-001/`

Minimum contents: Scenario ID · business path · preconditions · live steps · expected outcomes · related-domain re-run triggers · last-run log.

## Agent behaviour

1. Identify or create the Scenario Pack before claiming module completion.  
2. Prefer live observable business outcomes over verify-script Pass.  
3. On related-domain change: name the Scenario Pack(s) to re-run; treat prior certification as stale until Pass.  
4. On Scenario Fail: module status = **OPEN**; report Fail honestly; do not soft-close on engineering gates.  

